schedule.desc:
Long gone are the days when most fanfiction authors (and other fanwork creators) felt the need to keep this hobby hidden. Now, creators discuss fanwork and engage with fellow fans openly, sometimes attaching their real names, faces, and lives to their fannish content. How and when did this change? Is this entirely a positive development, or are there still good reasons to maintain some discretion?<br />
<br />
Companion panel to &quot;Freedom in Anonymity.&quot;
